(6764490, 1012198, 77196, '<td valign="top">Interesting photo. I like the texture and feel of the wood and windows. Yet, rather than have an "old" feel to it, the - to my mind at least - modern elements, like cinder blocks (concrete blocks), and plastic window coverings put it within my lifetime, losing the "nostalgic charm" factor.</td>', 'Interesting photo. I like the texture and feel of the wood and windows. Yet, rather than have an "old" feel to it, the - to my mind at least - modern elements, like cinder blocks (concrete blocks), and plastic window coverings put it within my lifetime, losing the "nostalgic charm" factor.', '2012-05-09 10:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6764493, 1012177, 144365, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by marabu61:</b></div><hr/><i> interesting, what is it? </i></td></tr></table> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jomari:</b></div><hr/><i> One of the most interesting and appealing. (What is it?) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It''s the title.  It''s the ROM (Royal Ontario Museum).  <br/>I never even thought to shoot this for the challenge.  Nice job and good thinking.<br/> <br/>CS <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by marabu61: interesting, what is it?  Originally posted by jomari: One of the most interesting and appealing. (What is it?)  It''s the title.  It''s the ROM (Royal Ontario Museum).  I never even thought to shoot this for the challenge.  Nice job and good thinking. CS ', '2012-05-09 10:17:23.000000', NULL, 0),
